  "worked_solution": "Splitting up the integral into the sum of two integrals and evaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2\\cdot {3}^{x}+x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2\\cdot {3}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}\u20613}\\,{|}_{0}^{1}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}\u20613}({3}^{1}-{3}^{0})+\\frac{1}{2}({1}^{2}-{0}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}\u20613}(3-1)+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}\u20613}+\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
